The white point for the selected calibration point, or -- with no row\nselected -- the value the next Anchor press captures.\n\nSet it until the picture looks right here, then Anchor. Move to very\ndifferent light and do it again: two points fix the buffer's real\nrelationship and the white point holds between them. Click a row below\nto come back and adjust that point; click it again to let go.	所选校准点的白点，或者——未选中任何行时——下次点击“在此处锚定”所捕获的值。\n\n调整它直到此处画面看起来正常，然后锚定。走到光照差异很大的地方再做一次：两个点可确定缓冲区的真实关系，白点会在两点之间保持正确。点击下方某行可返回调整该点；再次点击则取消选择。
A multiplier on the scan's white point, and the control you adjust between\nanchor points: dial it until the picture looks right in the current\nlight, then press Anchor here -- it captures the trimmed value as a new\npoint and resets the trim to 1.	扫描白点的乘数，也是在锚点之间调整的控件：调到当前光照下画面看起来正常，然后点击“在此处锚定”——它会把微调后的值捕获为一个新点，并将微调重置为 1。
A multiplier on the exposure the game supplied. 1.00x takes its number\nexactly, and that is the right answer here.\n\nThis is not a fudge factor. If a game needs the trim far from 1 to look\nright, that is evidence the exposure being read is wrong for that game,\nnot that the game wants trimming. Somewhere around 0.8 to 1.25 is honest\ntuning; reaching for 4 means something upstream is broken and the trim is\nhiding it.\n\nYour manual paper white is kept separately and comes back untouched if\nyou switch the option above off.	游戏所提供曝光值的乘数。1.00x 即原样采用该数值，这里这就是正确答案。\n\n这不是用来凑效果的系数。如果某个游戏需要远离 1 的微调才能看起来正常，说明读取的曝光值对该游戏是错的，而不是该游戏需要微调。0.8 到 1.25 左右是正常的调整；需要调到 4 则意味着上游有问题，而微调在掩盖它。\n\n你手动设置的纸白会单独保存，关闭上方的选项后会原样恢复。
What the frame is divided by before the model sees it. There is no other white\npoint; this is the whole of it.\n\nThe model was trained on finished frames where white sits at 1. The\nupscaler's output is linear and open-ended, so something has to say where\nwhite is -- and where the game's DLSS buffer is linear HDR, that number is\nrarely anywhere near 1. Measured in Monster Hunter Wilds it takes 16 or more\nbefore the model's detail reaches the frame at all, and the value that suits\na shaded camp is still too small for the same game out in daylight.\n\nToo low and almost every pixel trips the soft knee: the model is shown a\nflat near-white picture, its answer is scaled away, and only its hue\nsurvives -- which reads as a colour cast rather than as lost detail. Too\nhigh and it is shown an underexposed one, its answer degrades, and this same\nnumber multiplies that error on the way out.\n\nRaise it until the picture stops improving. Past that point it does not\nplateau, it gets worse in the other direction.\n\nThis was once a multiplier on a measured white point. The measurement is\ngone: it read scene brightness rather than where white belongs, handed the\nmodel a picture three times too dark, and left the highlight path nothing to\ngive back.\n\nAt strength zero the frame is still bit-identical whatever this says.	帧在交给模型之前所除以的数值。没有别的白点；这就是全部。\n\n模型是在已完成的画面上训练的，其中白色位于 1。放大器的输出是线性且无上限的，所以必须有东西指明白色在哪里——而当游戏的 DLSS 缓冲区是线性 HDR 时，这个数值很少接近 1。在《怪物猎人：荒野》中实测，需要 16 或更高，模型的细节才会真正体现在画面上；而适合阴影中营地的值，对于同一游戏的日光场景仍然太小。\n\n设得太低，几乎每个像素都会触发软拐点：模型看到的是一幅平淡、接近全白的画面，它的结果被缩放掉，只剩色相——看起来像偏色，而不像丢失了细节。设得太高，模型看到的是曝光不足的画面，结果变差，而且这个数值会在输出时把误差同样放大。\n\n逐步调高，直到画面不再改善。超过这个点后不会保持平稳，而是朝另一个方向变差。\n\n这里曾经是作用于测量白点的乘数。该测量已被移除：它读取的是场景亮度而不是白色应在的位置，交给模型的画面暗了三倍，让高光路径无从恢复。\n\n强度为零时，无论此值为何，帧仍保持逐位一致。
The most the pass may move any pixel, as a multiple of what it already was, in\nboth directions -- a pixel may not be brightened past this nor darkened past\nits reciprocal. Lights are where the model has least to say and rescaling its\nanswer does the most damage; 2x leaves detail intact while stopping a strip\nlight turning into a string of coloured cells. Raise it only if bright areas\nlook clipped.	本通道对任意像素改变的最大幅度，以其原值的倍数表示，双向生效——像素的提亮不能超过此值，压暗不能超过其倒数。光源是模型最没有发言权的地方，缩放其结果造成的损害也最大；2x 能保持细节完好，同时防止条形灯变成一串彩色方块。仅当明亮区域看起来被截断时才调高。
NVIDIA's highlight recovery, from RTX Remix. The model is shown everything\nbrighter than paper white squeezed into the top of its range, so its\nverdict there -- above all its colour -- is made without knowing how\nbright the pixel really is. This hands pixels that were very bright (one\nto eight times paper white) back to the game's own frame, a little at\nfirst and wholly at the top, so a fire keeps its orange and a coloured\nlight keeps its brightness.\n\nIt costs some of the model's detail in bright areas. Shadows and\nmidtones are untouched. Off is the composition as it always was.\n\nOnly offered on a linear HDR buffer, the one case where the model was\nshown a compressed picture.	NVIDIA 的高光恢复，来自 RTX Remix。比纸白更亮的所有内容都会被压缩到模型输入范围的顶部，因此模型在那里的判断——尤其是颜色——是在不知道像素实际有多亮的情况下做出的。此项会将非常亮的像素（纸白的一到八倍）交还给游戏自身的画面，开始时只交还一点，到顶部时完全交还，从而让火焰保持橙色，彩色灯光保持亮度。\n\n它会损失亮部区域的一部分模型细节。阴影和中间调不受影响。关闭时即为一贯的合成方式。\n\n仅在线性 HDR 缓冲区上提供，这是模型看到压缩画面的唯一情况。
A lamp in the corner: red for dark, green for full light, and the\nshades between, with the reading beside it.\n\nIt is how you see at a glance that the scan is TRACKING rather\nthan merely running. Walk into shade and it should slide toward\nred; step out and it should go green. If it moves the wrong way,\nthat is what the setting above is for.\n\nPurely a readout. It changes nothing.	角落里的一盏指示灯：红色表示暗，绿色表示全亮，中间为过渡色，旁边显示读数。\n\n通过它可以一眼看出扫描是在跟踪，而不只是在运行。走进阴影时它应滑向红色；走出来时应变绿。如果方向相反，就用上方的那个设置。\n\n纯粹是读数显示，不改变任何内容。
Make the picture look right, then press this -- it captures the current look\nas a point. For the first point use the Paper white slider above; for\nevery point after, move to different light and use the Trim, which the\nAnchor then bakes into a new point.\n\nThe first press calibrates one point -- the white point then\nfollows the scan by ratio from there, as before. Walk into very\ndifferent light, set paper white again, and press it again: the\nsecond point pins down the buffer's real curve and everything\nbetween the two is right, not just near one anchor. Up to eight.\n\nThe table is per game and shareable: one person calibrates a game\nand the numbers are the same for everyone who takes the profile.	让画面看起来正常，然后点击此按钮——它会把当前效果捕获为一个点。第一个点用上方的纸白滑块调整；之后的每个点，走到不同光照下用微调调整，再由锚定将其固化为一个新点。\n\n第一次点击校准一个点——之后白点会像以前一样按比例跟随扫描。走到光照差异很大的地方，再次调整纸白并再次点击：第二个点会确定缓冲区的真实曲线，两点之间的一切都会正确，而不仅仅是一个锚点附近。最多八个点。\n\n该表按游戏保存且可分享：一个人校准某个游戏后，使用该配置文件的每个人得到的数值都相同。
