# 2026-10-13: the pulse metric (docs/dlssnr/design/pulse-metric.md): the control under Compare and its help.
Measure the light step	测量亮度阶跃
How far the picture's light moves from one frame to the next because of the edit: the\nchange of log2(output light / frame light), in stops, averaged over two seconds.\nFrames where the model ran and frames where model cadence carried its edit are kept\napart, so the step on the model's frames against the carried ones is the cadence's\npulse as a number. A still scene reads cleanest; a pan adds its own changes.\n\nOne small measuring pass a frame while on. Also logged every 10 seconds.	由于编辑，画面亮度从一帧到下一帧变化了多少：log2(输出亮度 / 帧亮度) 的变化量，以档 (stop) 为单位，取两秒平均。模型运行的帧与由模型节奏沿用编辑的帧分开统计，因此模型帧相对于沿用帧的阶跃就是节奏脉动的数值。静止场景读数最干净；平移镜头会叠加其自身的变化。\n\n开启时每帧额外一次小型测量通道。也会每 10 秒写入日志。
Light step: the measuring pass could not be built.	亮度阶跃：无法构建测量通道。
# 2026-10-13: model cadence smoothing (docs/dlssnr/design/cadence-smoothing.md): the control and its help.
Smooth the model's frames	平滑模型帧
Without it, each new answer of the model replaces the carried one on the frame the model runs,\nand the picture's light steps there every N frames: the pulse. With it, the new answer is walked\nin from the carried one over the whole interval, in N equal steps, and the mean light of what the\ncadence shows may move by at most 1.5 stops a second while the frame's own light holds still.\n\nOnly what is shown changes: the stored edit and the model's own history stay as the model made\nthem. The previous answer stays on screen, fading, for up to N-1 frames longer, which can trail a\nlittle where things move fast. Measure it with "Measure the light step" under Compare.	不开启时，模型的每个新结果会在模型运行的那一帧替换沿用的结果，画面亮度会在那里每 N 帧跳变一次：即脉动。开启后，新结果会在整个间隔内以 N 个相等步长从沿用结果逐步过渡，并且在帧自身亮度不变时，节奏所显示内容的平均亮度每秒最多变化 1.5 档。\n\n只改变显示的内容：保存的编辑和模型自身的历史保持模型生成时的样子。上一个结果会在屏幕上逐渐淡出，最多多停留 N-1 帧，在快速移动处可能留下轻微拖尾。可用“比较”下的“测量亮度阶跃”来测量。
# 2026-10-13: the residual limit (docs/dlssnr/design/residual-limit.md): the control and its help.
Residual limit	残差限制
The most the model may move any pixel's light, either way, in stops: 0.5 allows\nat most 1.41x brighter or darker, 1 at most 2x. Off at 0, the composition as\nit always was.\n\nAimed at blotches and flicker: a patch of wall the model brightens by a stop\none frame and not the next. It bounds the model's real corrections the same\nway, so start high and lower it until the blotches go. It sits inside the\nhighlight guard and can only narrow it.	模型可以使任意像素亮度向上或向下改变的最大幅度，以档为单位：0.5 最多允许变亮或变暗 1.41x，1 最多 2x。设为 0 时关闭，即一贯的合成方式。\n\n针对斑块和闪烁：例如模型在某一帧把一片墙面提亮一档，下一帧却不提亮。它也会同样限制模型的真实校正，因此请从高值开始，逐步降低直到斑块消失。它位于高光保护之内，只能使其更窄。
# 2026-10-13: HDR10 and scRGB at present (docs/dlssnr/design/hdr-present-conversion.md): the switch, its readout, its
# Paper white, its timing line, and the reasons the conversion gives in the readout.
HDR output (HDR10 and scRGB)	HDR 输出（HDR10 和 scRGB）
The game presents in HDR: HDR10 (PQ, Rec.2020) or scRGB (linear light). Off, its\nframes are shown as the game rendered them and the pass does not run on them.\n\nOn, each frame is decoded to linear light, the pass runs on it as on any HDR\nframe, and it is encoded back with the game's own frame as the reference: every\npixel the pass leaves alone -- the interface, at strength zero -- keeps its exact\ncode. The model uses the display's Windows SDR white level times Paper white,\nor 203 nits when the display query is unavailable.\n\nExperimental: not yet measured on a real HDR display. HLG, studio-range or YCbCr\nPQ and other colour spaces stay declined.	游戏以 HDR 呈现：HDR10（PQ、Rec.2020）或 scRGB（线性光）。关闭时，其帧按游戏原本渲染的样子显示，本通道不会在其上运行。\n\n开启时，每一帧被解码为线性光，本通道像处理任何 HDR 帧一样在其上运行，然后以游戏自身的帧为参考重新编码：本通道未改动的每个像素——界面，以及强度为零时——都保持完全相同的编码值。模型使用显示器在 Windows 中的 SDR 白色亮度乘以纸白，若无法查询显示器则使用 203 尼特。\n\n实验性：尚未在真实 HDR 显示器上测量。HLG、演播室范围或 YCbCr 的 PQ 以及其他色彩空间仍不受支持。
HDR10	HDR10
scRGB	scRGB
%s, SDR white %.0f nits x %.2f	%s，SDR 白色 %.0f 尼特 x %.2f
Off: this %s swapchain is shown as the game rendered it.	关：此 %s 交换链按游戏原本渲染的样子显示。
Paper white (x the display's SDR white)	纸白（x 显示器的 SDR 白色）
The same Paper white as on any other frame, measured here against the display's\nSDR white shown above: 1.00 uses that value. Raise it if the\ngame's own HDR paper white is set brighter, lower it if darker. It changes what\nthe model is shown, not the frame where the pass leaves it alone.	与其他任何帧上相同的纸白，此处相对于上方显示的显示器 SDR 白色来衡量：1.00 即使用该值。如果游戏自身的 HDR 纸白设置得更亮就调高，更暗就调低。它改变的是模型看到的内容，而不是本通道未改动的帧。
HDR conversion, outside the dispatch: %.3f ms = %.3f ms decode + %.3f ms encode (sample %llu, %.1f s since recording)	HDR 转换，在 dispatch 之外：%.3f ms = %.3f ms 解码 + %.3f ms 编码（样本 %llu，录制后 %.1f s）
the swapchain's format is typeless, which the HDR conversion does not take; the frame is shown as the game rendered it	交换链格式为 typeless，HDR 转换不接受；该帧按游戏原本渲染的样子显示
nothing is known about this swapchain's colour space, and the HDR conversion does not guess; the frame is shown as the game rendered it	对此交换链的色彩空间一无所知，HDR 转换不会去猜测；该帧按游戏原本渲染的样子显示
the swapchain changed format after its colour space was set, and the HDR conversion waits for it to be set again; the frame is shown as the game rendered it	交换链在设置色彩空间后更改了格式，HDR 转换会等待其重新设置；该帧按游戏原本渲染的样子显示
the swapchain's colour space was recorded for another format; the frame is shown as the game rendered it	交换链的色彩空间是为另一种格式记录的；该帧按游戏原本渲染的样子显示
the swapchain is PQ in studio range or YCbCr, which the HDR conversion does not take; the frame is shown as the game rendered it	交换链为演播室范围的 PQ 或 YCbCr，HDR 转换不接受；该帧按游戏原本渲染的样子显示
the swapchain is ten-bit with a linear (scRGB) colour space, which the HDR conversion does not take; the frame is shown as the game rendered it	交换链为 10 位且使用线性 (scRGB) 色彩空间，HDR 转换不接受；该帧按游戏原本渲染的样子显示
